			"Message": "style(Maintain): Suppress lints in build script\n\nAdd `#![allow(...)]` directives to `build.rs` to silence `non_snake_case`, `non_camel_case_types`, `non_upper_case_globals`, `dead_code`, and unused variable/import warnings.\n\nThis aligns the build script's lint suppression strategy with the main crate in `Library.rs`, consolidating crate-level allowances and preventing a noisy build output from generated or placeholder code within the build process.",
			"SHA": "934e9db306fc5938a8f9075cb6748d39786e2b05"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:22:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				65,
				4
			],
			"Message": "style(Maintain): Suppress dead_code and unused variable warnings\n\nRemove redundant `#[allow(dead_code)]` attributes from `Guard::Note` and `start_hot_reload_watcher` by enabling `dead_code`, `unused_imports`, `unused_variables`, and `unused_assignments` at the crate level in `Library.rs`.\n\nThis aligns the compiler suppression strategy with the project's non-public API surface and placeholder implementations, ensuring a cleaner build output without scattering attributes across modules. The hot-reload watcher remains a stub for future functionality.",
			"SHA": "802f9154e0f3718e91050f265cc557ee42b69c1f"
		},
		{
